{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cfnxr5t19ZfJFYKhGAGJY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Based on this task, here are the concrete issues I encountered:\n\n1. **ToolSearch loads schema but doesn't invoke** — Most critical. Using `ToolSearch(\"select:mcp__sauce__sauce_skill\")` repeatedly just returned the tool schema without actually calling it. No clear guidance that you must then call the tool directly or use an agent to invoke it. The workflow is confusing: load → then what?\n\n2. **MCP server instructions truncated** — The sauce MCP guidance in the system reminder cuts off mid-sentence (\"**WRITE EACH PROGRAM YOURSELF**, in SauceScript, for the task as asked. The skills write the sauce command as `sauce <command>`: ... [rest missing]\"). Can't read the full vision.\n\n3. **Kitchen/Pot framing is EVM-centric** — The MCP instructions and sauce-overview conflate EVM (Pot contract, Kitchen.cook, callbacks) with Solana (Pot account, Kitchen program, CPIs). A Solana newcomer expecting Kitchen docs would get confused because most Kitchen details don't apply to Solana. Solana section needed earlier and more distinct.\n\n4. **No concrete example: how to invoke deferred tools** — After loading a schema with ToolSearch, no documented pattern for \"then call it like this.\" Had to infer via trial and error that agents could invoke them, or that Bash might work. Direct invocation syntax is never shown.\n\n5. **\"Use provided code as-is\" vs \"write yourself\" sounds contradictory** — sauce-solana-distributed-swap says use the example code as-is, but also says write each program yourself. Turns out: venue-specific byte layouts (swapV2 instruction IDs, account order) are the \"as-is\" part; control flow (which slots, refund logic) is what you write. This distinction is buried in the skill, not prominent upfront.\n\n**Recommendation**: Make ToolSearch documentation explicit that it only loads schema; show how to invoke the tool after. Separate Solana patterns from EVM in the overview. Show one concrete example of calling an MCP tool after loading it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41455,"cache_read_input_tokens":18287,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41455},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9ecd4db7-8a69-4ba2-9b9d-81f2228a7b8a","uuid":"0f00d2e7-7969-4614-a1b7-d74fc46d8479","timestamp":"2026-10-07T13:34:48.094Z","request_id":"req_011Cfnxr5eN9t5pFSHo2KXS1"}
